## Context

0151 keystone exit criterion: "Committed `tickets/erg` is byte-reproducible
from source; a CI check rebuilds the recorded revision and diffs it." No
`make verify` target exists today. The build embeds wall-clock `buildDate` and
`vcsRevision` via `-ldflags -X`, so a naive rebuild never matches. The target
must recover the committed binary's stamps (via `erg version` output or by
checking out the embedded revision) and re-inject them.

Secondary: `go.mod` says `go 1.21` with no `toolchain` directive; the host
has go1.22.2. Cross-machine byte-equality requires pinning. Add a `toolchain`
directive.

## Relevant files
- `Makefile` — build flags, `GO_LDFLAGS` (single source of truth)
- `src/go/go.mod` — needs `toolchain` directive
- `src/go/version.go` — `selfHash`, `readVersionInfo` (extract stamps)
- `tickets/erg` — the committed bootstrap binary to verify against

## Actions
1. Add `toolchain go1.22.2` to `src/go/go.mod` (pin to current host version).
2. Add a `verify` target to `Makefile` that:
   a. Reads `buildDate` and `vcsRevision` from `tickets/erg version` output.
   b. Rebuilds with those exact stamps: same `GO_BUILD_ENV`, `GO_BUILD_FLAGS`,
      `-ldflags` with the recovered values instead of `$$(date)` / `$$(git rev-parse)`.
   c. Compares SHA-256 of the rebuild against `tickets/erg`.
   d. Prints PASS/FAIL with both hashes.
3. Add `test-verify` to `TEST_SUITES` and a `tests/test_verify.sh` that runs
   `make verify` and asserts PASS.

## Test
```sh
# Red: make verify should exist and pass
make verify
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `make verify` rebuilds the committed binary with recovered stamps and
      reports PASS when hashes match
- [ ] `go.mod` has a `toolchain` directive pinning the Go version
- [ ] A test suite (`test-verify`) exercises the target
- [ ] `make test` passes
